    {
      "heading": "Reading rules",
      "text": [
        "The built-in vowel अ is not said at the end of a word (घर [ɡʱəɾ], not ɡʱəɾə), except after a conjunct (मित्र [ˈmit̪ɾə]). In the middle of longer words it is often dropped too; the pronunciation under each word shows which.",
        "च and ज are said ch and j before i, e and y (आजी, जेवण), and ts and dz before other vowels in Marathi words (आजोबा, चहा). Words from Sanskrit and English keep ch and j (चित्र, जून).",
        "इ/ई and उ/ऊ are spelling distinctions only: they sound the same.",
        "Stress is light and falls on the first syllable; the IPA marks it with ˈ."
      ]
    },
